            <ArticleTitle>Immunoblastic lymphadenopathy presenting as an acute abdomen and mixed bacteremia with Eikenella corrodens and group C streptococci.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>652-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eikenella corrodens and group C streptococci have been noted to occur with increased frequency in patients with underlying malignancies and immunosuppressive states. We report a case where these organisms were isolated from a patient with immunoblastic lymphadenopathy and discuss the possible association between these two conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
